        <mxCell id="gapbox" value="" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8cecc;strokeColor=#b85450;strokeWidth=2;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="920" width="1160" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gapbox_t" value="Two structural facts this diagram exists to make obvious" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=13;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#9c2b25;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="72" y="930" width="600" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="gapbox_c" value="1. The Ecosystem trait seam is half-built.  traits.rs declares it, pypi implements it, and cargo and npm ignore it:&#10;   each holds a concrete upstream client and calls unpack directly. docs/operations.md lists this as a known defect.&#10;   The consequence is not theoretical: the per-ecosystem paths duplicate structure that a finished seam would share.&#10;&#10;2. scan/coordinator.rs is deliberately one primitive, not two.  The same single-flight machinery deduplicates a&#10;   concurrent AI review and a concurrent plugin run, keyed by artifact identity. A FinishGuard is constructed first&#10;   on every path, so a panic inside the guarded work can never leave a key permanently stuck for later requests.&#10;&#10;One edge looks wrong and is not: policy -> ai exists only because policy/mod.rs imports COLLECTOR_VERSION and&#10;PROMPT_VERSION from ai to fold them into the fingerprint. It is a version-string dependency, not a check dependency." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=Courier New;fontSize=10;fontColor=#1a1a1a;spacingLeft=2;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="72" y="958" width="1130" height="105" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
